CORE
getopt.sh
--resolve-dynamic-sites --shell-max-arguments 2 --unwind 5
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[shell-unsupported\.1\] .* GETOPT_COMPATIBLE is not set where getopt outputs options .*: FAILURE$
^\[shell-argument-count\.1\] .* the output of getopt has at most --shell-max-arguments \(2\) words: FAILURE$
^\[shell-dynamic-site\.1\] .*: SUCCESS$
^\[shell-unsupported\.2\] .* the parts of the text of eval for the holes of "set -- "\* .*: SUCCESS$
^\[assertion\.1\] .* "an option or --": SUCCESS$
^\[\.unwind\.0\] .*: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
With refined strings, the output is any string (making it of its words
did not finish), while its fields are those of the words, so that the
loop still sees only options and --.
